<title>BANGLADESH: Bangladesh taka ends up on higher dollar supply.</title>
<headline>Bangladesh taka ends up on higher dollar supply.</headline>
<dateline>DHAKA 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bangladesh taka strengthened slightly against the U.S. dollar in interbank trading on Thursday as supply for the dollar rose, dealers said.</p>
<p>The taka closed at 42.5320/5420 per dollar against the previous close at 42.5360/5440.</p>
<p>The interbank call money rates closed unchanged at 3.75 percent to 4.25 percent.</p>
<p>-- Dhaka Newsroom +880-2-506363</p>
</text>
